            "review_title": "Review at Rex Hotel",
            "review_text": "William J\nSacramento14 contributions\n0\nAn elegant piece of history, with excellent service\nNov 2019\nI would recommend this hotel to anyone going to Ho Chi Minh City, partly for the history that took place here, partly for the excellent location, and also for the outstanding service. But keep in mind there are more modern, high rise, \"nicer\" hotels nearby. What the other hotels lack is the history, boutique feel, amazing staff, but they do have newer facilities. For example, our room had beautiful wood floors and furniture but an old worn-out sofa and curtains, our daughter's room had a leak somewhere that was slightly buckling the floor and made the room smell moldy.\n\nBreakfast is superb, there are live shows in the hotel, as well as luxury shopping, several rooftop pools, access to private drivers and guides, etc. But if you prefer modern, functional luxury to old world luxury, you might be happier elsewhere.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten November 6, 2019",
