            "review_title": "Review at Rex Hotel",
            "review_text": "Brian M\nLondon, United Kingdom18 contributions\n1\nNot Good!\nAug 2019 • Couples\nWent for the terrace bar after reading about it in a guide book. Only go for the view at this bar if you must. This place purports to be high end. However, have low expectations of drinks and service. My wife thought she would have a treat of a small bottle of champagne. It came, plastic cork, flat and warm. When we complained, it was not responded to well. We were begrudgingly offered a glass of wine instead. It came, small and even warmer. Had to add ice to it and then it was so watery. I ordered a gin and tonic. 25 minutes later, the gin came with a tin of tonic. With around eight staff and not many more customers, what took so long!!!!\nThe food menu was uninspiring so we didn’t bother. \nWe were then charged for the champagne, even though we sent it back. We were told it was to keep the accounts straight. That was a very expensive small Glass of warm, watery wine. \nThe view is good but go somewhere else instead. It is the only place we have had bad service in Vietnam.\nRead more\nWritten August 23, 2019",
